{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "CUDA Tile and torch.compile LLM/primitives inventory: 78 case variants across 16 operation names, 36 operation/shape contracts and 51 operation/shape/dtype contracts. Math policies, ranking algorithms and schedules are separate variants, not independent workloads.",
  "contracts": [
    "Use the same exported inputs, FP64 oracle and per-element bounds for native and torch.compile. Explicit fast_math does not relax the oracle.",
    "Group dtype, math policy, ranking algorithm and tile schedule separately. All pairings must also match shape, seed and input pattern.",
    "attention keeps FP32 probabilities; attention_tensorcore uses the declared narrow-probability common envelope and retains the secondary strict validation result.",
    "Native sort/topk preserve original-index ties. The standard Torch baseline allows tie permutations while checking sorted values, source indices and uniqueness; stable Torch is a separate contract.",
    "scan is inclusive unordered_tree, not ordered fold-left. repeated_extrema Top-K uses disjoint read-only input/output allocations, as provided by the harness.",
    "For graph performance use adaptive_replay_span_v2 on both implementations and retain all samples, replay counts, calibration and actual spans. Compare to older timing protocols separately.",
    "Compilation, correctness failures and timeouts are retained and excluded from runtime ratios. This inventory declares no performance result."
  ],
